  "brief": "River waking up — expressive Indian flute. 120 seconds, approximately 78 BPM, gentle 4/4. Lead bansuri with tanpura, delicate tabla and occasional santoor. Begin with a spacious flute introduction, introduce a graceful recurring melody, then develop it with ornamentation, breath-shaped phrases and a few fluid runs. Tabla should support the flute without crowding it. End by returning quietly to the opening idea. No voices. Aim for the warmth and expressive playing we loved in Yamuna at Dawn.",
